---
/* ============================================================================
   Google Analytics 4 (gtag.js), loaded after the page is idle
   ============================================================================
   Foundation, edit with care.

   Ported from nixoncreativestudio, which carries the canonical version of this
   component. Keep the two in step.

   WHY IT IS NOT THE SNIPPET GOOGLE HANDS YOU. Google's copy-paste block is
   `<script async src=".../gtag/js?id=...">` in the head, which puts ~100KB of
   third-party JavaScript in front of the render. This repo gates LCP as a HARD
   error at 4500ms and the home page has already failed that gate for smaller
   reasons (see lighthouserc.json's notes). So the dataLayer + gtag() stub are
   defined immediately, and the library itself is fetched AFTER the load event,
   at idle. Anything that calls gtag() before it arrives is queued, not lost.

   Nothing about page views changes: GA4 records the view when the script
   arrives, a second or so later.

   Building the <script> element at runtime rather than printing a literal tag
   also means Cloudflare Zaraz cannot silently swallow the call if a Zaraz tool
   is ever enabled on this zone. Zaraz rewrites literal googletagmanager tags in
   the HTML and, when it breaks, drops them with no error anywhere. There is no
   Zaraz on stonesteps50k.com today; this is the cheap insurance, and it is why
   two other sites in this family lost weeks of data.

   Rendered by BaseLayout only when PUBLIC_GA_ID looks like a real Measurement
   ID. Its own component because prettier-plugin-astro cannot parse a <script>
   nested inside a template expression; BaseLayout keeps the condition and this
   file keeps the script at the top level.
   ============================================================================ */

interface Props {
  /** The GA4 web data stream Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX). */
  gaId: string;
}
const { gaId } = Astro.props;
---

<script is:inline define:vars={{ gaId }}>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  // gtag.js requires a real `arguments` object here (it type-checks it), so
  // rest parameters would silently break every queued call.
  function gtag() {
    // eslint-disable-next-line prefer-rest-params
    window.dataLayer.push(arguments);
  }
  window.gtag = gtag;
  gtag('js', new Date());
  gtag('config', gaId);

  function loadGa() {
    var s = document.createElement('script');
    s.async = true;
    s.src = 'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=' + encodeURIComponent(gaId);
    document.head.appendChild(s);
  }
  function whenIdle() {
    if ('requestIdleCallback' in window) requestIdleCallback(loadGa, { timeout: 4000 });
    else setTimeout(loadGa, 500);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'complete') whenIdle();
  else window.addEventListener('load', whenIdle, { once: true });
</script>
